WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.291 --> 00:00:02.393
(hip hop music)

00:00:02.393 --> 00:00:04.058
- [Narrator] In Toronto,
there's a basketball fan

00:00:04.058 --> 00:00:05.378
like no other.

00:00:05.378 --> 00:00:07.765
- [Man] I breathe, drink,

00:00:07.765 --> 00:00:10.329
everything about the Raptors basketball.

00:00:10.329 --> 00:00:11.229
- [Narrator] He's truly--

00:00:11.229 --> 00:00:14.979
- My whole life is around
the Raptors season.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:17.007
- [Narrator] Deeply.

00:00:17.007 --> 00:00:18.898
- [Man] For the last 22 years

00:00:18.898 --> 00:00:21.508
I've never missed a game.

00:00:21.508 --> 00:00:24.175
- [Narrator] A Raptors superfan.

00:00:32.385 --> 00:00:36.423
- My name is Nav Bhatia
and I'm Raptors superfan.

00:00:36.423 --> 00:00:37.400
- [Narrator] If you've
watched any Raptors games

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.301
in the last decade,

00:00:38.301 --> 00:00:40.981
maybe you've noticed the
bearded man sitting courtside.

00:00:40.981 --> 00:00:42.829
Well, that's Nav and his
story starts in India

00:00:42.829 --> 00:00:45.759
and takes him right here to Canada.

00:00:45.759 --> 00:00:48.413
Fleeing violence, Nav left
and settled in Toronto.

00:00:48.413 --> 00:00:51.354
He worked hard, opened a very
successful car dealership,

00:00:51.354 --> 00:00:52.900
and when the city got
it's own NBA franchise--

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:57.779
- The Raptors arrived and I
bought my first two tickets.

00:00:57.779 --> 00:00:59.716
I enjoyed the game.

00:00:59.716 --> 00:01:03.299
I was cheering the most
in the whole arena.

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:08.260
- [Narrator] The team embraced him

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:09.870
and being a superfan has it's perks.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:12.054
- When the legend, Kobe Bryant,

00:01:12.054 --> 00:01:14.924
came for his last game to Toronto,

00:01:14.924 --> 00:01:19.271
he came to me and said,
"Superfan, I want to thank you.

00:01:19.271 --> 00:01:23.663
"What you have done because
you have created a culture

00:01:23.663 --> 00:01:25.903
"of bringing everybody together through

00:01:25.903 --> 00:01:27.722
"this game of basketball."

00:01:27.722 --> 00:01:29.813
- [Narrator] He also gets to
hang with Canadian royalty.

00:01:29.813 --> 00:01:33.192
- [Nav] I know Drake pretty well.

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:34.256
- [Narrator] But what's
most important about

00:01:34.256 --> 00:01:36.942
Nav's superfandom is that he
represents the changing face

00:01:36.942 --> 00:01:38.872
of basketball fans around the world.

00:01:38.872 --> 00:01:42.541
- Basketball has changed
my life tremendously.

00:01:42.541 --> 00:01:46.752
It has given me an
opportunity to integrate

00:01:46.752 --> 00:01:49.335
my community, the south Asians,

00:01:50.248 --> 00:01:51.988
into the mainstream.

00:01:51.988 --> 00:01:53.761
- [Narrator] Nav may be
the first Raptors superfan

00:01:53.761 --> 00:01:55.848
but he wants everyone on board.

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:59.662
- I want to see this game
taken to the next level

00:01:59.662 --> 00:02:00.993
where all the communities,

00:02:00.993 --> 00:02:04.956
everybody, the Sikhs,
the Hindus, the Muslims,

00:02:04.956 --> 00:02:07.373
everybody coming to the game.

